Theorem 22.Theorem:
Let $a, b \in \mathbb{R}^{+}$, and let us denote
$$
Q M=\sqrt{\frac{a^{2}+b^{2}}{2}}, \quad A M=\frac{a+b}{2}, \quad G M=\sqrt{a b} \quad \text { and } \quad H M=\frac{2}{\frac{1}{a}+\frac{1}{b}}
$$

Then
$$
\begin{equation*}
Q M \geq A M \geq G M \geq H M \tag{2.1}
\end{equation*}
$$

Equalities occur if and only if $a=b$.

Theorem 24.Theorem:
Let $x_{i}, i=1,2, \ldots, n$, be real numbers with the same sign, greater then -1 . Then we have
$$
\begin{equation*}
\left(1+x_{1}\right)\left(1+x_{2}\right) \cdots\left(1+x_{n}\right) \geq 1+x_{1}+x_{2}+\cdots+x_{n} \tag{4.1}
\end{equation*}
$$

Theorem 31.Theorem:
Let $a_{1}, a_{2}, \ldots, a_{n} ; b_{1}, b_{2}, \ldots, b_{n}$ be real numbers. Then
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \sqrt{a_{1}^{2}+b_{1}^{2}}+\sqrt{a_{2}^{2}+b_{2}^{2}}+\cdots+\sqrt{a_{n}^{2}+b_{n}^{2}} \\
& \quad \geq \sqrt{\left(a_{1}+a_{2}+\cdots+a_{n}\right)^{2}+\left(b_{1}+b_{2}+\cdots+b_{n}\right)^{2}}
